1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,140
What choice do we have?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,550
The world is a cruel place!

3
00:00:15,590 --> 00:00:19,690
I swore... to kill them all!

4
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:22,250
Every last one!

5
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:26,430
And just like that...

6
00:00:26,430 --> 00:00:28,177
Everything changed.

7
00:00:31,022 --> 00:00:34,088
At that terrible moment, in our hearts, we knew.

8
00:00:37,088 --> 00:00:41,355
Home was a pen. Humanity... cattle.

9
00:00:58,230 --> 00:00:59,290
Eren!

10
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:01,700
Eren...

11
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:07,860
O, my friend!

12
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:10,460
This is a victory for us!

13
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:13,620
Our fame starts here!

14
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:14,620
O, my friend!

15
00:01:14,620 --> 00:01:19,920
Let us celebrate this victory
for the next battle!

16
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:40,100
"I died for naught" — I won't
let it end like that for you

17
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:45,360
until I am the last one standing

18
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:48,340
The enemy is cruel... We will kill...

19
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:51,380
The enemy is colossal... We will jump...

20
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:55,020
In our hands we hold blades of glory

21
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:57,300
and sing in the name of victory

22
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:01,940
We bear the wings of freedom on our backs

23
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:09,380
Swearing iron determination upon our hearts,

24
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:13,920
we slash apart the circle of idiocy

25
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:17,820
and soar through the sky

26
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:22,080
with our wings of freedom

27
00:02:36,010 --> 00:02:41,020
Wall: Assault on Stohess, Part 3

28
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:43,700
brothers and sisters.

29
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:49,390
Let us pray for the continued
strength of saints Maria, Rose, and Sina.

30
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:51,650
May they stand firm.

31
00:02:52,410 --> 00:02:55,470
Their grace is a manifestation
of our good faith...

32
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:58,920
We give thanks to the light
of the divine architect.

33
00:02:58,950 --> 00:03:00,920
He whose wisdom is the mortar;

34
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:05,860
whose sublime love for his
creation is the steadfast stone.

35
00:03:05,890 --> 00:03:08,290
He, and he alone, protects us from

36
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:12,100
the Titan scourge, in proportion
to our worship.

37
00:03:12,130 --> 00:03:15,700
Verily... innocence and
obedience are all he asks...

38
00:03:25,010 --> 00:03:28,140
No! Impossible!

39
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:43,330
Dear God! Please! Not the wall!

40
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:45,460
Stay away!

41
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:09,690
Well I daresay it looks like our boy's
in control of himself this time.

42
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:12,650
Yeah. Still, though...
There's no guarantee

43
00:04:12,650 --> 00:04:14,880
this will turn out any differently
than their last meeting.

44
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:17,960
Come on, he
wouldn't have transformed...

45
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,430
Unless he knew he could take her this time...

46
00:04:20,470 --> 00:04:21,900
He's got this, okay?

47
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:22,650
I don't doubt that.

48
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:24,890
But determination alone isn't
enough to win a fight.

49
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:26,940
You of all people should know that.

50
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:31,040
It'll take more
than that to beat Annie.

51
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,540
A lot more.

52
00:04:34,610 --> 00:04:35,590
Damn it!

53
00:04:36,510 --> 00:04:38,350
She's making a
break for level ground!

54
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:40,850
So much for our gear! What now?

55
00:04:41,410 --> 00:04:43,350
Split into two
teams and go around!

56
00:04:43,390 --> 00:04:44,570
Understood!

57
00:04:51,210 --> 00:04:52,460
C'mon, c'mon, c'mon!

58
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:54,720
Son of a... where'd
they come from?

59
00:05:13,990 --> 00:05:17,650
Annie... always so cynical...

60
00:05:17,690 --> 00:05:21,030
Like every little thing around you
was pointless.

61
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:25,320
Nothing
worth a second look.

62
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:31,670
Every now and then, though, I
could see through the act...

63
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:35,420
Especially when you were showing
off your fighting skills.

64
00:05:35,810 --> 00:05:38,480
Maybe hand-to-hand
combat didn't count for squat

65
00:05:38,510 --> 00:05:41,220
against our final
grade back at the academy...

66
00:05:41,410 --> 00:05:45,450
But to you? It was a
different story altogether.

67
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:48,690
Yeah... about that much at least.

68
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:51,790
It was
obvious you were a liar.

69
00:05:52,690 --> 00:05:54,560
Fighting's your whole world,

70
00:05:54,630 --> 00:05:57,460
but what exactly
are you fighting for?

71
00:05:57,530 --> 00:06:02,220
What could possibly have been worth
all this death and destruction?!

72
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:26,590
Oh, God...

73
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:28,360
Section commander, I hate to say it,

74
00:06:28,390 --> 00:06:30,790
but the city'll be debris
and corpses before long...

75
00:06:30,830 --> 00:06:32,560
Even if we manage to catch her.

76
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,060
Well, then that's how it's gonna be!

77
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:36,630
We're sticking to commander
Erwin's plan, got it?

78
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,060
So stop babbling
and ready the nets.

79
00:06:39,090 --> 00:06:40,260
Right.

80
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:45,340
Eren...

81
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:47,790
We didn't
sign up for this.

82
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:51,660
They... they didn't say there'd be
Titans fighting in the streets.

83
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:53,650
No kidding. This is crazy.

84
00:06:54,850 --> 00:06:57,030
We've got two of 'em
hashing it out in the streets?

85
00:06:57,470 --> 00:06:58,120
Yes, Sir.

86
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:00,990
The city's collapsing
like a house of cards.

87
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:03,330
It's just... it's horrifying...

88
00:07:03,390 --> 00:07:05,860
We can only guess
how many casualties...

89
00:07:06,930 --> 00:07:10,670
Erwin! Your arrogance has
brought hell right to our door!

90
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:12,240
I know.

91
00:07:15,610 --> 00:07:18,170
I acted entirely
on my own authority.

92
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:20,550
And I offer no excuses.

93
00:07:24,420 --> 00:07:27,180
You knew what this would
do to us, you son of a bitch!

94
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:29,350
You knew and
our lives be damned!

95
00:07:29,390 --> 00:07:31,780
Why? Damn you, why?

96
00:07:36,730 --> 00:07:38,180
For humanity.

97
00:07:39,030 --> 00:07:40,630
For victory.

98
00:07:40,670 --> 00:07:42,180
don't give me that!

99
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:44,330
You're nothing but a traitor!

100
00:07:44,370 --> 00:07:46,650
I ought to kill you right here and now!

101
00:07:46,650 --> 00:07:48,720
None of the higher ups would fault me!

102
00:07:49,970 --> 00:07:52,140
Do as your
conscience dictates.

103
00:07:52,210 --> 00:07:54,180
My post is yours.

104
00:07:54,350 --> 00:07:56,570
The female Titan must not escape.

105
00:07:56,570 --> 00:08:00,730
Deployment is through peer and
Beirer is in command of provisions.

106
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,150
Work with them closely.

107
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:04,090
Do whatever is required
to ensure she doesn't...

108
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:05,320
Shut up!

109
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:09,270
Do... do you really believe...

110
00:08:09,290 --> 00:08:12,230
...this is for the good of us all?

111
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:14,680
I have faith it's a step forward.

112
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:22,140
Everyone, lower your rifles.

113
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:24,040
Place this man under arrest.

114
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:24,840
Sir!

115
00:08:25,780 --> 00:08:27,780
Deploy all troops immediately.

116
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:31,350
As of now... focus on evacuation.

117
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:32,990
Yes, Sir!

118
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:35,100
Erwin...

119
00:08:35,130 --> 00:08:38,760
I hereby wash my hands of you and
leave you to the high court.

120
00:08:38,890 --> 00:08:41,750
I'll accept their judgment. Thank you, nile.

121
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:44,740
Levi. For now, stay here.

122
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:46,920
A pointless death wouldn't suit you.

123
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:48,860
No, I doubt it would...

124
00:08:49,470 --> 00:08:51,570
Any more than it suits anyone else.

125
00:08:57,840 --> 00:09:03,100
To rise above monsters, we
have to abandon our humanity.

126
00:09:04,010 --> 00:09:06,770
What we fight, we become...

127
00:09:10,090 --> 00:09:11,820
...fire with fire.

128
00:09:16,260 --> 00:09:18,830
Look at her.
Annie can do it.

129
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:26,010
Annie...

130
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:28,730
Annie!

131
00:09:49,330 --> 00:09:50,540
Annie...

132
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:54,800
I believe in you.

133
00:09:54,830 --> 00:09:57,170
I'm always on your side.

134
00:10:12,750 --> 00:10:18,810
I... will... kill them...

135
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:22,600
Every last one!

136
00:10:47,250 --> 00:10:48,730
Eren!

137
00:10:51,490 --> 00:10:53,220
What is he...?

138
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:54,880
Help him!

139
00:10:54,910 --> 00:10:57,060
No! With the state he's in,

140
00:10:57,060 --> 00:10:59,160
it's probably best that
we keep our distance.

141
00:11:16,310 --> 00:11:17,810
God.

142
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:46,910
She's headed up the wall!

143
00:11:46,910 --> 00:11:48,430
She's trying to escape!

144
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:04,360
No, no, no! We can't let her get away!

145
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:07,800
I won't let her!

146
00:12:22,980 --> 00:12:24,380
It's over, Annie.

147
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:27,250
Now fall.

148
00:12:35,690 --> 00:12:36,790
Annie...

149
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:40,160
I'm so sorry.

150
00:12:41,370 --> 00:12:44,070
I don't
expect you to forgive me.

151
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:48,510
But... please...

152
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:50,820
Please just...

153
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:57,920
Stand your ground. Stand your ground

154
00:12:57,920 --> 00:13:00,620
even if the whole world stands against you.

155
00:13:02,350 --> 00:13:08,390
Die... all of you... everything...

156
00:13:08,430 --> 00:13:10,430
They'll despise you...

157
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:12,650
They won't understand.

158
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:16,860
But I will. Your dad always will.

159
00:13:17,970 --> 00:13:21,410
Oh, no! He's gonna devour her whole!

160
00:13:21,410 --> 00:13:22,660
Eren! Back off!

161
00:13:22,660 --> 00:13:23,530
don't do it!

162
00:13:23,530 --> 00:13:27,410
This... is freedom!

163
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:30,310
Promise me you'll return...

164
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:33,120
That's all I ask.

165
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:53,710
Wha... what's he doing?

166
00:13:56,370 --> 00:13:57,680
Son of a...?

167
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,110
They're merging?

168
00:14:10,450 --> 00:14:11,800
Stop it, Eren!

169
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:21,660
It's not a good idea
to eat our key evidence...

170
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:23,400
You idiot.

171
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:12,780
Eren.

172
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:16,890
Mikasa... is Annie...?

173
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:30,230
Damn it!

174
00:15:30,730 --> 00:15:33,880
All the shit we've been through
and this is what we get?

175
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:36,780
Annie! Wake up!

176
00:15:36,830 --> 00:15:39,460
C'mon, face the
music! You owe us!

177
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:43,220
don't be a coward!
I know you can hear me!

178
00:15:45,330 --> 00:15:46,530
That's enough.

179
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:49,340
It's over.

180
00:15:54,310 --> 00:15:56,480
Someone get me a wire net!

181
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:58,880
This thing belongs
deep underground!

182
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:00,140
Understood!

183
00:16:01,670 --> 00:16:03,430
What have we done?

184
00:16:03,470 --> 00:16:08,200
If we can't get any answers out of her,
then what was the point of all this?

185
00:16:08,590 --> 00:16:11,530
We're left with nothing
but countless casualties,

186
00:16:11,530 --> 00:16:14,770
ruined lives,
and unanswered questions.

187
00:16:14,770 --> 00:16:16,540
All for what?

188
00:16:27,130 --> 00:16:28,990
Well, it was a valiant effort.

189
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:30,980
Can't win 'em all though, right?

190
00:16:30,980 --> 00:16:31,730
Right.

191
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:35,360
At the very least the scout
regiment's been exonerated.

192
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:38,100
Sure, by the skin of its teeth, but still.

193
00:16:40,050 --> 00:16:42,180
Let's hope the brass agrees.

194
00:16:51,750 --> 00:16:55,420
As you might imagine,
we have many questions.

195
00:16:56,660 --> 00:16:59,490
If the target's identity
was beyond all doubt,

196
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:03,110
why would you neglect to request
aid from the military police?

197
00:17:03,110 --> 00:17:05,990
Discretion. We had
reason to believe she was

198
00:17:05,990 --> 00:17:08,250
operating in conjunction
with other insiders.

199
00:17:08,250 --> 00:17:12,570
I felt it was necessary to involve
only those well above suspicion, Sir.

200
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:16,810
Yes. And the price of your "discretion"
was the near obliteration of Stohess.

201
00:17:16,840 --> 00:17:17,900
Well done.

202
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:20,540
I didn't foresee
the damage's scale, Sir.

203
00:17:20,850 --> 00:17:22,280
Blame my incompetence.

204
00:17:22,310 --> 00:17:24,320
Blame isn't going to rebuild my roof!

205
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:26,320
If the female Titan
were left to roam free...

206
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:28,310
The wall was subject to breach...

207
00:17:28,330 --> 00:17:31,190
And the damage to Stohess
would've been beyond devastating.

208
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:32,520
Perhaps.

209
00:17:32,690 --> 00:17:33,720
Erwin...

210
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:36,660
You have me grasping at
straws to exonerate you...

211
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:40,830
What I need is proof that your tactics
yielded some manner of benefit.

212
00:17:40,870 --> 00:17:44,300
Granted, Annie Leonhart is
rendered innocuous,

213
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:46,640
but also essentially useless.

214
00:17:46,670 --> 00:17:49,170
Yes, Sir. That she is.

215
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:50,700
Are you saying...

216
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:53,130
It was all for nothing...?

217
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:00,090
Hey.

218
00:18:09,330 --> 00:18:10,890
You feel okay?

219
00:18:12,910 --> 00:18:13,630
Yeah...

220
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:18,210
In fact it's weird how "okay" I feel.

221
00:18:20,090 --> 00:18:23,400
So, is... Annie still stuck in that thing?

222
00:18:23,890 --> 00:18:25,160
Uh-huh.

223
00:18:25,610 --> 00:18:28,440
Yeah... you'd think after all we sacrificed

224
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:30,480
to get her back, fate
would cut us a little slack.

225
00:18:30,550 --> 00:18:34,320
It's humbling, knowing how far
she'll go to keep her secrets.

226
00:18:34,390 --> 00:18:37,740
Humbling? More like infuriating.

227
00:18:38,170 --> 00:18:40,300
Why'd you let her go, Eren?

228
00:18:44,270 --> 00:18:46,450
You did... didn't you?

229
00:18:47,550 --> 00:18:49,160
You gave her an out.

230
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:54,670
I know. I didn't mean to, I...

231
00:18:54,710 --> 00:18:56,810
I just couldn't help it.

232
00:18:58,340 --> 00:19:02,090
When I saw her face, I just froze...

233
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:08,480
Armin Arlelt, and Jean Kirschtein...

234
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:09,850
You two are up first.

235
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:10,920
Yes, Sir.

236
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:12,560
Debriefing time.

237
00:19:12,590 --> 00:19:14,120
See you later, I guess.

238
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:15,430
Sure.

239
00:19:27,640 --> 00:19:31,450
Honestly... it felt kinda... good.

240
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:34,380
Just letting go...

241
00:19:34,410 --> 00:19:37,160
My body, my mind, everything...

242
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:40,120
For a minute it was almost...

243
00:19:40,190 --> 00:19:41,950
Like I wanted to die...

244
00:19:42,020 --> 00:19:43,630
Eren, stop it!

245
00:19:46,690 --> 00:19:48,930
don't worry,
I'm better now.

246
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:00,740
I'm glad...

247
00:20:02,170 --> 00:20:04,080
I'm glad you're back...

248
00:20:09,650 --> 00:20:11,950
I can't get my head wrapped around it.

249
00:20:11,980 --> 00:20:16,090
This whole fighting fire with
fire business or whatever.

250
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:18,660
Is that really the
only option we've got?

251
00:20:18,890 --> 00:20:22,590
Not necessarily. Just the only
one that's presented itself.

252
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:25,660
And now we know Eren can do it.

253
00:20:27,970 --> 00:20:32,890
Yeah, well... if it's that easy for the
fight to turn us all into monsters...

254
00:20:33,710 --> 00:20:36,060
...then maybe we don't deserve to win.

255
00:20:46,990 --> 00:20:48,230
Go on.

256
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:10,010
No one ever promised us
we'd come out of this unscathed.

257
00:21:10,870 --> 00:21:14,610
For nothing? I believe this latest tragedy

258
00:21:14,610 --> 00:21:17,340
has moved us forward
by leaps and bounds, Sir.

259
00:21:20,750 --> 00:21:22,650
Not long ago, we hadn't even imagined

260
00:21:22,690 --> 00:21:25,790
the possibility of humans
transforming into Titans.

261
00:21:25,820 --> 00:21:28,560
Now, we're not only aware of
the enemy in our midst...

262
00:21:28,690 --> 00:21:30,590
We've managed to capture one of them.

263
00:21:30,660 --> 00:21:35,940
Make no mistake, there are more out there.
And we will hunt down every last one.

264
00:21:36,570 --> 00:21:38,330
The initiative is ours.

265
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:40,170
Starting now...

266
00:21:41,488 --> 00:21:44,032
We launch an attack on
the Titans within our walls!

267
00:21:48,750 --> 00:21:53,680
The scout regiment's recall to the capital
and Eren's incarceration were rescinded.

268
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:57,720
Instead, they were charged with guarding
Annie Leonhart in her holding cell

269
00:21:57,760 --> 00:22:01,790
deep underground, where they
kept strict vigil day and night.

270
00:22:02,430 --> 00:22:03,960
Sadly, however...

271
00:22:04,030 --> 00:22:06,430
It would
take a far longer time...

272
00:22:06,460 --> 00:22:08,800
And cost a
great many more lives...

273
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:13,820
for humanity to discover the true nature...
of what it held captive.
